    "letter": "c",
    "value": "1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1978-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The condition is \\[ 4\\left(\\frac1{2\\pi r}\\right)=2r. \\] Multiplying by \\(\\pi r\\) gives \\(2=2\\pi r^2,\\) so the area \\(\\pi r^2\\) equals \\(1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the circumference and diameter in terms of the radius \\(r\\)",
        "The condition directly determines the product \\(\\pi r^2\\)"
      ],
